From: MyszkinPL <211237936+MyszkinPL@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: a64: enable PLL lock detection

The PLL lock bits (bit 28 of each PLL control register) only report lock
when the matching enable bit in PLL_LOCK_CTRL (0x320, bits 0-12) is set.
The vendor boot firmware of the Yandex Station 1 leaves all of them clear
(the register reads 0x10000000), so every rate change of a PLL waits the
whole 70 ms timeout in ccu_helper_wait_for_lock() and warns, e.g. on each
cpufreq transition of PLL-CPUX.

Verified on the board: with bits 0-12 set, every running PLL (CPUX,
VIDEO0, PERIPH0, MIPI, HSIC, DE, DDR1) reads locked, disabled ones read
unlocked, and cpufreq transitions complete without the timeout.

Signed-off-by: MyszkinPL <211237936+MyszkinPL@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-a64.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-a64.c
@@ -165,6 +165,9 @@
  */
 #define SUN50I_A64_PLL_MIPI_REG		0x040
 
+#define SUN50I_A64_PLL_LOCK_CTRL_REG	0x320
+#define SUN50I_A64_PLL_LOCK_ENABLE_ALL	GENMASK(12, 0)
+
 static struct ccu_nkm pll_mipi_clk = {
 	/*
 	 * The bit 23 and 22 are called "LDO{1,2}_EN" on the SoC's
@@ -959,6 +962,15 @@
 
 	writel(0x515, reg + SUN50I_A64_PLL_MIPI_REG);
 
+	/*
+	 * The PLL lock bits only report lock when enabled here; some boot
+	 * firmware leaves them all off, and every PLL rate change would then
+	 * wait out the 70 ms lock timeout and warn.
+	 */
+	val = readl(reg + SUN50I_A64_PLL_LOCK_CTRL_REG);
+	writel(val | SUN50I_A64_PLL_LOCK_ENABLE_ALL,
+	       reg + SUN50I_A64_PLL_LOCK_CTRL_REG);
+
 	ret = devm_sunxi_ccu_probe(&pdev->dev, reg, &sun50i_a64_ccu_desc);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
